Damn, it was just starting to get good.

325
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,920
Hey, Drake, I'm curious.

326
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:30,202
How many people have you killed?

327
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:33,700
Trafalgar Law, the Surgeon of Death.

328
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:36,760
His bounty is 200 million berries.

329
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:42,137
As you know, a countless number of
pirate crews have entered the Grand Line,

330
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:44,632
but only a handful have made it this far.

331
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:48,666
The Grand Line is basically an
enormous tournament of survival,

332
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:51,557
regardless of which path
they took to get here.

333
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,680
The ones that made it are
the cream of the crop.

334
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:58,217
I'd even go so far as to say
that one of them might go

335
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:01,712
on to become the leader of the
next generation of pirates!

336
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:03,317
So fair warning!

337
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:06,597
With this many rookies passing
the red line at the same time,

338
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:09,297
Things are bound to get
quite ugly in the new world.

339
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:10,210
Also,

340
00:16:10,293 --> 00:16:13,857
in case you're wondering why Captain
Kidd's bounty is so much higher than yours?

341
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:17,737
It's because he has no qualms
with attacking innocent civilians.

342
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:19,777
Not very charming, huh?

343
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:21,537
I prefer you boys.

344
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:23,267
You can count on my support.

345
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,558
I'll be cheering for you all the way

346
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,014
Thanks, but I gotta be honest with you.

347
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,880
I'm just trying to have fun

348
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:36,617
But you do have me a little
afraid for the old coding

349
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:39,641
mechanic pirate guy this
town sounds pretty rough.

350
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,620
Oh you've got nothing to worry about.

351
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,540
Trust me Rayleigh's all right.

352
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:48,035
He's a hundred times stronger than you

353
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:51,540
did she say a hundred times

354
00:16:55,880 --> 00:17:00,437
you ready chomper yeah just so you
know i'm sure the navy is aware that

355
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:04,217
all you up and coming heavy-hitting
pirates have made landfall here i'd

356
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:09,497
keep an eye out for anything suspicious
if i were you now that's not good

357
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:13,577
so you're saying they could strike
at any time from out of nowhere Yes,

358
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:15,997
but you might be in luck
in addition to the usual

359
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:18,557
troublemakers around
these parts With all the

360
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:21,017
other pirates landing
here at the same time Navy

361
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:24,041
headquarters probably has
its hands full right now

362
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:27,437
Unless something especially
problematic happens

363
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:30,077
the Navy won't waste major
military resources on

364
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:32,937
checking it out In other
words keep your heads down

365
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:35,557
try not to cause any trouble
and you should be fine.

366
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,470
Okay?

367
00:17:36,553 --> 00:17:37,383
Sure I understand.

368
00:17:37,466 --> 00:17:38,360
Thanks a lot.

369
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,913
You are a real big help

370
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:53,160
I'm telling you they were crazy strong
sounds like you had a rough time?

371
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:57,277
So what's this proposition of yours right

372
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:00,397
I'm sorry sir you see
master peterman I think

373
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:02,377
the Girl with Straw Hat luffy might be a

374
00:18:02,460 --> 00:18:05,342
mermaid I noticed something
when I saw her before

375
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:15,637
After she fell to the ground her shoe came

376
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:19,360
off when it did I saw
a fin instead of a foot

377
