the middle of the street?

500
00:26:03,240 --> 00:26:04,877
Don't he know you don't
do that around here?

501
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:07,136
He's going to cause a lot of trouble.

502
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:18,437
Hey, what's the matter?

503
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:20,932
Do you need some directions or something?

504
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:30,471
What in the hell does he think he's doing?

505
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:40,880
A kid?

506
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:46,430
Oh!

507
00:26:46,513 --> 00:26:47,343
Big Brother!

508
00:26:47,780 --> 00:26:49,340
Why'd you have to die?

509
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:51,840
Why'd you leave me? Nooo!

510
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:54,420
Just stay still, tough guy.

511
00:26:55,620 --> 00:26:56,450
Oh!

512
00:26:56,533 --> 00:26:57,363
Big Brother!

513
00:26:57,600 --> 00:27:00,237
Why'd you stand up to a Celestial Dragon?

514
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:02,680
You know they can only end in death!

515
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:06,860
I guess I actually sought him, huh?

516
00:27:07,620 --> 00:27:10,057
Thought for sure he
dodged at the last second,

517
00:27:10,140 --> 00:27:12,434
but oh, well, must be imagining things.

518
00:27:16,540 --> 00:27:17,880
Well, whatever.

519
00:27:18,320 --> 00:27:19,560
As long as he's dead.

520
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:38,197
What the heck were you
thinking attacking a

521
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:40,717
celestial dragon like that
you'll bring admirals?

522
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:44,437
Here what's with all this
tomato juice it's to make you

523
00:27:44,520 --> 00:27:47,177
look dead and unless you want
to be that way for real mr.

524
00:27:47,260 --> 00:27:49,077
troublemaker you better obey the unwritten

525
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:53,657
pirate rules what are you
talking About hey? Wait a minute!

526
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:54,797
There was a kid here.

527
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:55,737
Where'd she go?

528
00:27:55,820 --> 00:27:58,977
Don't get the rest of us
caught up in your trouble!

529
00:27:59,060 --> 00:28:00,537
Are you messed up in the head?

530
00:28:00,620 --> 00:28:01,450
No, I'm fine.

531
00:28:01,533 --> 00:28:02,363
I didn't hit my head.

532
00:28:02,446 --> 00:28:03,276
You numbskull!

533
00:28:03,359 --> 00:28:05,597
I'm talking about the inside! Jeez!

534
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:06,557
What a dumbass!

535
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:08,157
How have you survived this long?

536
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,070
Well?

537
00:28:09,153 --> 00:28:09,983
Thanks to jewelry!

538
00:28:10,066 --> 00:28:10,896
Barney over there!

539
00:28:10,979 --> 00:28:12,417
We managed to avoid the
worst case scenario!

540
00:28:12,500 --> 00:28:14,877
That man is pirate on Azoro! A member?

541
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:16,237
of the Straw Hat Pirates.

542
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:19,537
I heard their crew was kind of
wild, but attacking a dragon!

543
00:28:19,620 --> 00:28:22,032
and in a public street in broad daylight?

544
00:28:22,660 --> 00:28:23,980
That's plain bonkers.

545
00:28:24,180 --> 00:28:26,277
It's only natural that he was saved.

546
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:29,377
I didn't see the shadow of
death upon him at this time.

547
00:28:29,460 --> 00:28:30,740
I felt his bloodlust.

548
00:28:30,980 --> 00:28:33,357
That guy will cut you down
without a second thought.

549
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,780
He's a real monster.

550
00:28:35,020 --> 00:28:37,340
A bounty of 120 million berries.

551
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:40,957
Doesn't seem like a lackey, but
he's number two on the Straw Hats.

552
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:43,417
I guess that goes to show
the caliber of his captain.

553
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:46,720
Right, so, where's the
nearest hospital? Hospital?

554
00:28:46,900 --> 00:28:48,312
This man needs a doctor.

555
00:28:48,580 --> 00:28:50,760
He took a bullet. What? Forget him.

556
00:28:50,920 --> 00:28:52,220
He's a total stranger.

557
00:28:53,420 --> 00:28:55,067
You've got to be kidding me.

558
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:57,340
A pirate helping out some random guy?

559
00:28:57,540 --> 00:28:58,893
Never seen that before.

560
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:09,640
I saw something when I went into town.

561
00:29:09,840 --> 00:29:11,977
These bubble bicycle
things were flying around.

562
00:29:12,060 --> 00:29:14,680
Yeah, I saw those, too. Pretty cool, huh?

563
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:15,757
We should buy a couple.

564
00:29:15,840 --> 00:29:18,546
I bet you those bikes
have a real smooth ride.

565
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:19,630
The snail.

566
00:29:19,713 --> 00:29:20,543
It's probably Nami.

567
00:29:21,940 --> 00:29:22,770
Click.

568
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:25,377
Hello, my beautiful Nami! Sanji!

569
00:29:25,460 --> 00:29:27,342
Sanji and Chopper, listen to me!

570
00:29:28,300 --> 00:29:33,241
Basically, they had so many kinds of ice
cream, we got caught up and made a mistake!

571
00:29:33,420 --> 00:29:35,417
Slow down, you're not making any sense.

572
00:29:35,500 --> 00:29:37,620
No, Sanji, it's terrible! Terrible!

573
00:29:37,900 --> 00:29:39,240
What are we gonna do?

574
00:29:40,700 --> 00:29:45,360
I don't know what you're saying calm
down just start over what's going on

575
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:11,477
We don't even have a clue what kidnapter.

576
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:13,120
This place is gigantic.

577
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:14,777
We need to split up and start...

578
00:30:14,860 --> 00:30:15,690
Don't move.

579
00:30:15,773 --> 00:30:17,277
Tell me exactly where you are.

580
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:19,017
We'll come and meet you there.

581
00:30:19,100 --> 00:30:20,197
But we...

582
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:24,221
We know some experts when it comes
to this sort of thing, remember?

583
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:27,900
I'm calling in the Flying Fish Riders.

584
00:30:28,900 --> 00:30:29,730
What?

585
00:30:33,780 --> 00:30:34,610
Yahoo!

586
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:36,337
Handsome's here.

587
00:30:36,420 --> 00:30:37,250
Oh, I'm sorry.

588
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:38,397
I mean, Duval's here.

589
00:30:38,480 --> 00:30:39,720
So are we!

590
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:42,640
How are you, young Master Blackleg?

591
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:45,557
Angry, because you fish
riders took too long!

592
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:48,397
We're not fish riders anymore,
young Master, you remember?

593
00:30:48,480 --> 00:30:50,820
We're the Rosie Life Riders now.

594
00:30:51,480 --> 00:30:52,917
You're freaking annoying, okay?

595
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:54,037
That's what you are!

596
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:55,317
It's our mermaid friend.

597
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:57,580
She got kidnapped in Sabaody Park.

598
00:30:57,800 --> 00:30:59,741
I called you to help us find her.

599
00:31:00,020 --> 00:31:01,100
Not kidnappers?

600
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:02,120
How horrible!

601
00:31:02,420 --> 00:31:04,361
They sound like devious villains!

602
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:07,137
You guys were kidnappers
too, like what, yesterday?

603
00:31:07,220 --> 00:31:09,357
They say it takes a thief to catch one.

604
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:10,360
So here we are.

605
00:31:10,560 --> 00:31:11,397
Are you guys up for this?

606
00:31:11,480 --> 00:31:12,310
But of course.

607
00:31:12,393 --> 00:31:14,137
We shall do our very best to serve you.

608
00:31:14,220 --> 00:31:15,677
Your wish is our command.

609
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:17,417
Can we really trust these guys?

610
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:22,206
Oh, and by the by, before I came here, I
showed off my new looks to some ladies.

611
00:31:22,620 --> 00:31:25,796
I wasn't quite the success
that I imagined I would be.

612
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:28,957
Well, I can fix your
face, but not your brain.

613
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:30,746
Or your annoying personality.

614
00:31:30,940 --> 00:31:32,175
But that's all right.

615
00:31:32,280 --> 00:31:33,400
I'll help you out.

616
00:31:33,580 --> 00:31:34,417
Don't you worry.

617
00:31:34,500 --> 00:31:37,737
We just need to find your mermaid
friend before she gets sold, right?

618
00:31:37,820 --> 00:31:38,650
You got it.

619
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:39,977
Since you're from around here,

620
00:31:40,060 --> 00:31:42,697
I figure you must know the
archipelago better than us.

621
00:31:42,780 --> 00:31:44,080
Why, of course we do.

622
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:45,557
Sabo Odi is our backyard.

623
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:47,346
We know all the ins and outs.

624
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:49,717
You won't find a better
tour guide than us.

625
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:51,180
Okay, hop on.

626
00:31:51,700 --> 00:31:53,406
We're taking the flying fish?

627
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:54,660
You bet we are.

628
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:56,417
Right, ready when you are.

629
00:31:56,500 --> 00:31:57,330
Right.

630
00:31:57,413 --> 00:31:59,277
Uh, how do you guys plan on finding her?

631
00:31:59,360 --> 00:32:00,400
Now, don't fret.

632
00:32:00,660 --> 00:32:04,017
Those of a trade know each other's ways,
and we were once kidnappers as well.

633
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:07,747
I can think of a few groups
already that might be responsible.

634
00:32:09,680 --> 00:32:10,510
First off,

635
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:12,737
we'll take a quick cruise
across the groves and pick up

636
00:32:12,820 --> 00:32:14,997
the rest of your crew so they
can help with the search.

637
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:16,021
In the meantime,

638
00:32:16,280 --> 00:32:20,280
we'll try and find out which
kidnappers grabbed your mermaid friend.

639
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:22,550
Let's go!

640
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:23,800
Full speed ahead!

641
00:32:25,420 --> 00:32:26,250
Yeah!

642
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:32,100
I hope this works out.

643
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:34,657
Sanji, what now?

644
00:32:34,740 --> 00:32:36,380
It's gonna be okay.

645
00:32:36,760 --> 00:32:38,777
Just stay right there
and don't move an inch.

646
00:32:38,860 --> 00:32:40,637
I'll send someone there to get you.

647
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:41,550
Okay.

648
00:32:41,633 --> 00:32:42,463
Calic.

649
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:46,190
Luffy!

650
00:32:46,273 --> 00:32:47,220
Sanji says not to go!

651
00:32:51,620 --> 00:32:52,760
Just to be safe,

652
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:56,357
we should still wait here instead
of breaking up the group even more.

653
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:57,852
Don't you think, Brooke?

654
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:14,617
Let me put it this way Sanji gave us very

655
00:33:14,700 --> 00:33:16,877
specific instructions
to stay here and wait

656
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:19,217
for someone to come
pick us up and no matter

657
00:33:19,300 --> 00:33:22,000
what we do our wait will be just as long?

658
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:34,680
Hey, head, we made it to
Sabaody Park. What's next?

659
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:38,017
Find the rest of the Straw Hats
and pick up one member each.

660
00:33:38,100 --> 00:33:38,930
Right.

661
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:46,277
They were supposed to wait by public
transponder snail number five,

662
00:33:46,360 --> 00:33:47,517
which should be right here.

663
00:33:47,600 --> 00:33:48,835
Yeah, there they are.

664
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,420
See, on the bench.

665
00:33:50,620 --> 00:33:52,561
It looks like Brooke and Chopper.

666
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:56,097
All right, you guys, we're ready to go.

667
00:33:56,180 --> 00:33:57,239
Hurry up, let's...

668
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,537
Why are you two so relaxed?

669
00:34:00,620 --> 00:34:01,561
This is serious!

670
00:34:03,360 --> 00:34:04,190
Let's go!

671
00:34:05,120 --> 00:34:07,767
Operation Save Kuma at
all costs is underway!

672
00:34:08,340 --> 00:34:09,170
Yes!

673
00:34:09,253 --> 00:34:10,260
Let's go all out!

674
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:11,380
No relaxing!

675
00:34:11,700 --> 00:34:14,100
But he got mad at us!

676
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:16,057
I knew it then, I regret it now!

677
00:34:16,140 --> 00:34:17,937
Just a little bit, but I regret it!

678
00:34:18,020 --> 00:34:21,197
Keep on the lookout for every
kidnapping team on the archipelago!

679
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:23,817
It's gotta be one of them, so
it's only a matter of time!

680
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:28,277
And I know the other Straw Hats ran
off, but we still got to find them, too.

681
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,190
Roger.

682
00:34:29,273 --> 00:34:30,320
Let's split up. Ride!

683
00:34:31,620 --> 00:34:33,397
We're betting our pride on this.

684
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:35,537
You better not let the young master down.

685
00:34:35,620 --> 00:34:37,679
Do this fast and do it right, okay?

686
00:34:38,500 --> 00:34:39,857
That should be good enough.

687
00:34:39,940 --> 00:34:40,897
Good enough for who?

688
00:34:40,980 --> 00:34:43,337
And can't you do something
about this slow-ass cow?

689
00:34:43,420 --> 00:34:45,857
If I'd have known it was like
this, I would have got on a fish.

690
00:34:45,940 --> 00:34:46,770
What?

691
00:34:46,853 --> 00:34:47,734
You said I'm handsome?

692
00:34:47,820 --> 00:34:48,702
Not even close.

693
00:34:48,980 --> 00:34:50,557
Also, you're the head of your gang.

694
00:34:50,640 --> 00:34:54,057
Why are you stuck on the slowest
ride when everyone else can fly?

695
00:34:54,140 --> 00:34:56,197
Why would you say something like that?

696
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:58,717
Of course I'm the most
handsome person on the team.

697
00:34:58,800 --> 00:34:59,857
There's no competition.

698
00:34:59,940 --> 00:35:01,757
Just shut up and step on it, okay?

699
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,000
Yes, young master.

700
00:35:06,860 --> 00:35:10,060
Do you swear no one came
here to sell a mermaid?

701
00:35:10,380 --> 00:35:11,837
Yeah, yeah, I swear it.

702
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:12,750
No one today.

703
00:35:12,833 --> 00:35:13,663
Stop it, Straw Hat.

704
00:35:13,746 --> 00:35:16,484
It'll only be harder on
us if you cause trouble.

705
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:20,057
Octoguy, let's look around the shop.

706
00:35:20,140 --> 00:35:20,970
Okay.

707
00:35:24,900 --> 00:35:25,730
Hey.

708
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:30,548
Did you guys have any luck?

709
00:35:30,860 --> 00:35:33,660
No, looks like he was
telling the truth. Jamie!

710
00:35:34,840 --> 00:35:36,020
Come on, Straw Hat.

711
00:35:36,180 --> 00:35:37,837
We're gonna have to look somewhere else.

712
00:35:37,920 --> 00:35:39,273
Hey, I just remembered.

713
00:35:39,500 --> 00:35:41,977
Now that you mention
it, I do have a mermaid.

714
00:35:42,060 --> 00:35:43,560
For real? Do you mean it?

715
00:35:43,700 --> 00:35:44,840
Yeah, but only one.

716
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,677
This pretty little thing here.

717
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:47,701
Her name's Mari.

718
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:50,217
If you like her, I'll
cut you guys a good deal.

719
00:35:50,300 --> 00:35:52,124
Don't you want to take me home?

720
00:35:52,420 --> 00:35:54,517
There's no way in hell that's a mermaid!

721
00:35:54,600 --> 00:35:56,953
I saw him in the shop just a second ago.

722
00:35:57,780 --> 00:35:59,898
It's really hard to breathe in here.

723
00:36:00,860 --> 00:36:01,690
Hey!

724
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:05,550
Kuma!

725
00:36:05,980 --> 00:36:07,200
Where are you?

726
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:09,497
You, don't lose hope.

727
00:36:09,580 --> 00:36:11,097
Maybe she hasn't been sold yet.

728
00:36:11,180 --> 00:36:14,356
We just gotta figure out
which kidnappers grabbed her.

729
00:36:14,460 --> 00:36:15,940
Hey, check it out.

730
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:18,777
That guy's Straw Hat Luffy
from the East Blue, isn't he?

731
00:36:18,860 --> 00:36:19,917
He's shorter than I thought.

732
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,897
This is all my fault.

733
00:36:21,980 --> 00:36:26,957
The amusement park is the number one
spot for kidnappers to pick people up.

734
00:36:27,040 --> 00:36:31,687
I knew they'd be on the lookout for a
mermaid like her but I didn't do a thing.

735
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:34,817
Whoa they've got all
kinds of ice cream here.

736
00:36:34,900 --> 00:36:36,937
What flavor do you want? Hold on.

737
00:36:37,020 --> 00:36:38,297
I gotta go see it for myself.

738
00:36:38,380 --> 00:36:39,997
I'll be right back.

739
00:36:40,080 --> 00:36:41,137
Kuma you wait here.

740
00:36:41,220 --> 00:36:43,557
Yeah. Okay.

741
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:45,157
But get something yummy for me too.

742
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:46,070
All right.

743
00:36:47,660 --> 00:36:51,097
I'm never going to see her again, and the
last thing I said was about ice cream.

744
00:36:51,180 --> 00:36:52,160
It's terrible.

745
00:36:53,660 --> 00:36:55,937
I never should have let her
go to that amusement park.

746
00:36:56,020 --> 00:36:57,196
What was I thinking?

747
00:36:57,900 --> 00:37:02,240
It's just, I've dreamed of this
moment ever since I was a little girl.

748
00:37:05,360 --> 00:37:07,697
I've never been so high
up in the air before.

749
00:37:07,780 --> 00:37:09,217
I'll always remember this day.

750
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:10,359
Thank you so much.

751
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:12,786
You didn't do anything wrong.

752
00:37:12,900 --> 00:37:14,477
She was really happy we got to go.

753
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:16,537
It's nobody's fault it
turned out like that.

754
00:37:16,620 --> 00:37:17,620
You don't get it.

755
00:37:17,940 --> 00:37:22,577
Truth is It's a terrible idea for fishmen
and merfolk to come to this place at all.

756
00:37:22,660 --> 00:37:25,817
But hachi he wanted to help you
guys after what you did for us.

757
00:37:25,900 --> 00:37:26,877
And I felt the same way.

758
00:37:26,960 --> 00:37:28,720
Papagu, don't say anymore.

759
00:37:29,060 --> 00:37:30,957
We're stuck like this
either way You might as

760
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:33,197
well tell me why it's so
bad for you to come here.

761
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:34,456
What's the big deal?

762
00:37:35,220 --> 00:37:36,102
The kidnappers.

763
00:37:36,220 --> 00:37:39,497
They're not the only enemies
Kuma and Hachi have in Sabo Odi.

764
00:37:39,580 --> 00:37:43,698
In fact You might say everyone in
the whole archipelago is their enemy

765
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:47,140
Two hundred years ago?

766
00:37:47,380 --> 00:37:49,757
Yes, it's more recent
than you would think.

767
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:52,037
But things used to be quite terrible here.

768
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:55,397
The fishmen and merfolk races
were considered the same as fish,

769
00:37:55,480 --> 00:37:59,177
and humans all over the world
